    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0547" n="423" xml:id="pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.77/256: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-05T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>109. Your No. 121, August 24, 1 p.m.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d329-f1"/></p>
                <p>Cable from American Embassy, Paris,<anchor n="42" xml:id="d329-f2"/> states that
                    Farnham considers authorization sufficient for negotiations with French
                    bondholders, but that it will be necessary for Government of Haiti definitely to
                    authorize issue of the bonds required in this transaction.</p>
                <p>Department assumes that law authorizing C bonds will be passed subsequently.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
